The candidate 8b7b3a4a7136ba671b5a448fc6c4626c7800f1dc was rejected
before lifecycle persistence because its detector overmatched eval arguments
after legitimate Deno subcommands. This final RED amendment defines both sides
of the bounded static boundary:

- eval as the Deno subcommand after supported global options, including quoted
  and quote-concatenated tokens, receives task_definition_noop;
- eval after run/test/check, in a path, filter, or argument, remains legitimate;
- a separate option value named eval is skipped before locating the subcommand;
- task text is never executed or generally shell-parsed by production.

